    "DateTime": {
      "name": "DateTime",
      "kind": "SCALAR",
      "fields": {},
      "desc": "A deliberately small, Linear-shaped GraphQL schema used to exercise every\nbranch of the GraphQL ingestion pipeline. NOT a copy of Linear's schema —\npurpose-built so the emitted goldens stay readable.\n\nCoverage:\n  - load / list / create / update / remove on Issue\n  - a command mutation (issueArchive) folded as an $action point\n  - Relay connection machinery (nodes + pageInfo) driving list pagination\n  - a deprecated field, excluded from the default fragment\n  - a scalar field with a REQUIRED argument, also excluded (selecting it\n    unbound would fail GraphQL validation)\n  - a to-one relation, reduced to an { id } stub\n  - a to-many relation (a connection on the type, not a root field)\n  - an enum, a custom scalar, and comparator-style filter inputs\n  - ragged op sets: Team has no mutations, Comment has create only"
    },
    "ID": {
      "name": "ID",
      "kind": "SCALAR",
      "fields": {},
      "desc": "The `ID` scalar type represents a unique identifier, often used to refetch an object or as key for a cache. The ID type appears in a JSON response as a String; however, it is not intended to be human-readable. When expected as an input type, any string (such as `\"4\"`) or integer (such as `4`) input value will be accepted as an ID."
    },
